#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""shipm-watch — finds frozen or stuck work (chats, agents, background jobs, leftovers) in every project and keeps the Mac healthy.

  shipm-watch scan [--dry]           one scan: writes ~/.local/state/shipmiracle/health.json (+ lineage.json), cleans what is provably safe (not with --dry)
  shipm-watch status                 human-readable summary of health.json
  shipm-watch host [--heavy-ok]      exit 0 if the Mac can take a heavy job (swap < 70 %, load < 1.5 x cores), else 1 and the reason
  shipm-watch can OP ID              {ok, why, project, kind, working}: is this step applicable right now (fresh raw scan, item still raised)?
  shipm-watch act OP ID              an action the owner clicked: {"ok":bool,"did":str,"why":str} (checked against a fresh scan and the live process first)
  shipm-watch act checkpoint PROJECT save uncommitted work to wip/frozen-<date> (git plumbing; the working tree is not touched); prints the branch
  shipm-watch verify ID              one scan without hysteresis: {gone, detail, checked, item, chat_state, working, interrupted_at, lead_mtime}
  shipm-watch contract               the registry (KINDS / OPS) as JSON

Every item kind is declared ONCE in KINDS below (mode auto | fix | info | wait, an ordered chain of OPS, texts); add() fills the item from it.
tests/health_contract_test.py fails the build for a kind without an entry. Quiet = no write in the chat's transcript or its agents' files.
Frozen = quiet AND no child process using CPU. A chat that waits for you, for a plan approval, for the usage limit, for the API or for a
background job is shown as that, never as frozen. Items appear after 2 scans in a row and disappear after 2 clean scans (info/auto at once).
Automatic: provably dead agent records and 'working' states (every scan), proven orphans, old task outputs, state files of projects that do not
exist. Never automatic: ending a live chat, agent or job. Scans, verify and act share one lock (STATE/watch.lock).
Env for tests (they count only when SHIPMIRACLE_TEST=1): SHIPMIRACLE_STATE SHIPMIRACLE_HOME SHIPMIRACLE_DEV SHIPMIRACLE_WS SHIPMIRACLE_NOW SHIPMIRACLE_PS (ps table file) SHIPMIRACLE_LSOF (json pid->cwd) SHIPMIRACLE_HOST (json host readings) SHIPMIRACLE_KILL_LOG
(record kills instead of killing) SHIPMIRACLE_TMP (task output root) SHIPMIRACLE_LOCK_WAIT (seconds to wait for the scan lock) SHIPMIRACLE_DOCKER (file: one 'name<TAB>compose working_dir' line per container; first line
ERROR = docker cannot be asked) SHIPMIRACLE_COLIMA (file: 'running' or 'stopped'; `colima stop` writes 'stopped' into it)."""
import datetime, fcntl, hashlib, json, os, pathlib, re, signal, subprocess, sys, time

